    "instructions": {
        "Presentations" : "<p> Students will work on a term project throughout the semester and present that project over three talks. </p>  <h2>Deliverable</h2> <p> By Sunday evening of the week of a presentation, students should submit their project in its most recent state as a single compressed (.zip) email attachment to the instructor. </p>    <h2>Talk</h2> Each talk will feature two primary, interwoven components: <ol style='padding-left:2.25em'> <li> <b>Demo.</b> Prepared demonstration / explanation. The student prepares this ahead of time. Counts towards the grade. </li> <li><b>QnA.</b> Dynamic question answering. Instructor initiated at various points during the demo. Student response assessed and considered toward grade assignment.</li> </ol> </p>      <p> Students will be in front of the class for equivalent amounts of time during each presentation. What will vary between students is the amount of time spent on <i>demo</i> versus <i>QnA</i>. Demos that are informative and engaging will likely involve / necessitate less QnA, so it is in a student's best interest to make the demo portion(s) as informative and engaging as possible.</p>  <h2>Durations</h2> <style> .durations-table { border-collapse: collapse; margin-left:2.25em; } .durations-table th, .durations-table td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding-left: 6px; padding-right: 6px; padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 6px; } .durations-table th { background: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; } .durations-table tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: #fafafa; } </style> <table class='durations-table'> <thead> <tr> <th>Presentation</th> <th>Duration</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>1: The Pitch</td> <td>4 min</td> </tr> <tr> <td>2: The Progress</td> <td>6 min</td> </tr> <tr> <td>3: The...Perfection?</td> <td>8 min</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>  <h2>Rubric</h2> <p> <style> .rubric-table { border-collapse: collapse; margin-left: 2.25em; } .rubric-table th, .rubric-table td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding-left: 6px; padding-right: 6px; padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 6px; } .rubric-table th { background: #f2f2f2; text-align: left; } .rubric-table tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: #fafafa; } </style> <table class='rubric-table'> <thead> <tr> <th></th> <th>2</th> <th>1</th> <th>0</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>Deliverable</strong></td> <td>On time, on pace.</td> <td>Fails one criteria.</td> <td>Fails two or more criteria.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Demo</strong></td> <td>Matches deliverable, clear, engaging.</td> <td>Fails 1 criteria.</td> <td>Fails 2 or more.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>QnA</strong></td> <td>Accurate answers, clear responses.</td> <td>Fails 1 criteria.</td> <td>Fails 2 or more.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </p> <br>    <h2>Notes</h2> <ol style='padding-left:2.25em'> <li>Time limits are firm. Practice with a timer.</li> <li>Presentation order will be randomly determined by instructor ahead of time.</li> <li>Have a plan B for demo failures (recording, second machine, etc). Recovering well counts.</li> <li>Slides/notecards fine. Scripts and pre-loaded AI answers are not.</li> </ol> </section>",
        "Progress reports" : "Here is an <i>HTML-syntax</i> string",
        "Semester project" : "Guess what? That's right! Another string!"
    }
